"G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.25,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'loaded once via projects_store.read_projects(repo_root) and threaded into compute_outbound_mutations as a new optional field on OutboundDiffConfig'","Plan also: 'It calls resolve_project(ticket, mapping)' and 'resolves to a key NOT in mapping.projects'","projects_store.py:116-118 read_projects returns load_mapping(repo_root).projects (a dict), not a Mapping","projects_store.py:97-110 resolve_project(ticket, mapping) reads mapping.legacy_default; projects_store.py:41 Mapping.projects is the dataclass field"],"finding":"On the differ side the plan loads the mapping via projects_store.read_projects(repo_root) yet then calls resolve_project(ticket, mapping) and checks membership in mapping.projects — but read_projects returns a bare dict[str, dict[str, Any]] (the .projects sub-map only), whereas resolve_project requires a Mapping object (it dereferences mapping.legacy_default at projects_store.py:106) and mapping.projects is an attribute of the Mapping dataclass (projects_store.py:41), not of a plain dict. As written the differ-side data flow cannot use read_projects's return value for both resolve_project and the .projects membership check.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fb3352aa2b5aca4fb","impact":0.85,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach → 'Create targets the ticket's resolved project' bullet; outbound_differ.py OutboundDiffConfig field","norm_id":"n03ba194b2e5078d6","priority":0.85,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A ticket with bridge_project absent must resolve to legacy_default, but a bare read_projects() dict carries no legacy_default, so the absent-field arm cannot be evaluated","Implementer wires read_projects() and then hits an AttributeError on .projects / a type error passing a dict where resolve_project expects a Mapping"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Use load_mapping(repo_root) on the d